###  https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#YarnHairiness
:YarnHairiness rdf:type owl:Class ;
               rdfs:subClassOf :YarnStructuralCharacteristic ;
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf> ;
               rdfs:comment "Yarn structural characteristic concerning fibre ends and loops protruding from the yarn body."@en ;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure> ;
               rdfs:label "Yarn hairiness"@en ;
               <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#evidenceStatus> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#explicitEvidence> ;
               <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "Table 180 identifies yarn hairiness as an unwanted yarn characteristic. It reports that hairiness decreases with increasing fibre length and fibre strength, while it may increase with fibre fineness after the optimal working range."@en ,
                                                                        "Yarn hairiness is modelled as a yarn structural characteristic rather than as an assessment result. Quantitative hairiness values, test methods or thresholds should be represented in the assessment module."@en ;
               <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceLocator> "JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.2, printed pages 488-491, lines 11875-11888; JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, Table 178, printed page 302; caption line 9109."@en ;
               <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceType> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition> .


